# Image TODO: hami-what-needs-real-gpu-v1.png

## Purpose
Draw the honest boundary of this lesson: what works on fake GPUs versus what needs a
real GPU (Lesson 6.4).

## Composition breakdown
- Split illustration, divided by a dashed vertical line labeled "the honest boundary".
- Left half (green background), headed "Works on fake GPUs (this lesson)": cards
  reading "capacity advertising", "HAMi scheduler + webhook", "scheduling chain /
  schedulerName rewrite", "pod reaches Running", "simulated nvidia-smi output".
- Right half (amber background), headed "Needs a real GPU (Lesson 6.4)": cards reading
  "real gpumem VRAM partition", "real gpucores compute limit", "OOM on over-request",
  "binpack vs spread packing", "CUDA execution".

